          %h2#references References
          %p The concept goes back to
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shigeo+Sasaki"}> Shigeo Sasaki
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On differentiable manifolds with certain structures which are closely related to almost contact structure I
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.tmj/1178244407"} euclid:1178244407
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shigeo+Sasaki"}> Shigeo Sasaki
                , Y. Hatakeyama,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On differentiable manifolds with contact metric structures
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.jmsj/1261060580"} euclid:1261060580
          %p An early set of lecture notes is
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shigeo+Sasaki"}> Shigeo Sasaki
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Almost contact manifolds, Part 1
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shigeo+Sasaki"}> Shigeo Sasaki
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Almost contact manifolds, Part 2
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shigeo+Sasaki"}> Shigeo Sasaki
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Almost contact manifolds, Part 3
          %blockquote
            %p
              Even today, after 40 years, the breath, depth and the relative completeness of the Sasaki lectures is truly quite remarkable.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
              As it is, the notes are not easily available and, consequently, not well-known. (
              %a{:href => "#BoyerGalicki07"}> Boyer-Galicki 07, p. 1
              )
          %p Modern accounts include
          %ul
            %li#BoyerGalicki07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Boyer"}> Charles Boyer
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Krzysztof+Galicki"} Krzysztof Galicki
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Sasakian Geometry
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.oxfordscholarship.com/view/10.1093/acprof:oso/9780198564959.001.0001/acprof-9780198564959"} doi:10.1093/acprof:oso/9780198564959.001.0001
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Boyer"}> Charles Boyer
                ,
                %em Sasakian geometry: The recent work of Krzysztof Galicki
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0806.0373"}> arXiv:0806.0373
                )
            %li#Sparks10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Sparks"}> James Sparks
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Sasaki-Einstein Manifolds
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1004.2461"} arXiv:1004.2461
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sasakian_manifold"} Sasakian manifold
          %p
            Discussion related to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structure"} spin structure
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82-structure"} G₂-structure
          %ul
            %li#AgFried10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ilka+Agricola"}> Ilka Agricola
              ,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Friedrich"} Thomas Friedrich
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  3-Sasakian manifolds in dimension seven, their spinors and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
                  structures
              %strong 60
              (2010) 326-332 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.geomphys.2009.10.003"}> doi:10.1016/j.geomphys.2009.10.003
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0812.1651"} arXiv:0812.1651
          %p
            Relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SU%282%29-structure"} SU(2)-structure
          %ul
            %li#CMD14
              %p
                Beniamino Cappelletti-Montano, Giulia Dileo,
                %em
                  Nearly Sasakian geometry and
                  = succeed "-structures" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi SU
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1410.0942"}> arXiv:1410.0942
                )
            %li#Fino18b
              %p
                Anna Fino,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Hypo contact and Sasakian structures on Lie groups
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Workshop on CR and Sasakian Geometry
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.uni.lu/CRSasaki/slides/fino.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion relating to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quiver+gauge+theories"} quiver gauge theories
            includes
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Olaf+Lechtenfeld"}> Olaf Lechtenfeld
              , Alexander Popov,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Szabo"} Richard Szabo
              %em Sasakian quiver gauge theories and instantons on Calabi-Yau cones
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1412.4409"}> arXiv:1412.4409
              )
          %p
            In
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+Figueroa-O%27Farrill"}> José Figueroa-O'Farrill
              , Andrea Santi,
